From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:15:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/13] proxy: `rules --json`, and `proxy run` with
 placeholders on WASI

`fnox proxy rules --json` prints the validated [proxy] configuration as
JSON, for tools that turn a project's rules into proposals. On WASI the
proxy command is built again without the local proxy: `proxy run --
cmd` gives the command each rule's sealed placeholder under the rule's
environment name, scrubs the other secrets and ambient credentials as
upstream does, and leaves injection to seven's realm proxy. A rule
whose secret is not sealed is refused. Rule validation no longer needs
reqwest on WASI.

